    Bug 2002937 - Link returned data to the sending window. r=mkmelin


    This is strange. The converted data is stored per window and there
    should not be a way to leak data from one `MsgOperationObserver` to
    another.

    We currently do not check the `tab`, which is send with the event.
    The only mechanism I could see is that the first window sends all
    its events twice, causing the listener waiting for the second
    window to receive the data for the first window again.

    This patch is adding the tab id to the message, causing the second
    part of the test waiting for "his" events. If we get the data for
    the first event twice, we should see that in the final report of
    unexpected messages.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D274389

